# Anchored at the context root unless it starts with `**/`, which is why the two
# node_modules trees and the several target dirs are written the wide way.
**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.env
.env.*
bowerbird.db
bowerbird.db-*
bowerbird.db.*
backups
# Where a checkout's own run puts every generated file (DATA_DIR's default), plus
# the pre-move layout that kept them under the library root.
data
**/.bowerbird
coverage
# Rust build artefacts, several GB of them per tree. The image builds the crate
# itself, so a host-built `librawshim.so` sitting at the path the loader checks
# first would shadow the image's own.
**/target
# Built by the image's own stages, from the version of the source the image has.
# A host copy arrives ahead of the build that would produce it: the `native`
# stage's `get-slangc.ts` finds a compiler and skips the fetch, `.codecs` is a
# symlink into the host's cache that `native` then copies the image's tree onto,
# and `COPY web ./web` lands host-built assets on top of the ones vite just wrote.
native/rawshim/.slangc
native/rawshim/.codecs
native/rawshim/pkg
web/dist
web/test-results
# Agent worktrees, a full checkout of this repo apiece.
.claude
.playwright-mcp
# A local photo library and the RAW test fixtures: hundreds of MB the image has no
# use for, and the integration tests do not run in it.
.photos
test/fixtures
